22	 * CSS Sanitizer that returns a DocumentFragment with sanitized content.
23	 *
24	 * The reason why this is not part of the HtmlSanitizer is to avoid a potential
25	 * misuse of the CSS Sanitizer that would break its security guarantees.
26	 *
27	 * The CSS Sanitizer uses Shadow DOM to isolate the sanitized content from the
28	 * rest of the page. It provides an encapsulation layer for stylesheets and
29	 * ensures that there are no clashes between ids or class names.
30	 *
31	 * If the CSS Sanitizer was part of the HtmlSanitizer, it would be possible
32	 * to call `sanitize` with a string that contains both HTML and CSS, which
33	 * wouldn't be nested inside a shadow DOM.
